//ERR 13 3 13 6
//MSG="This function does not return a value in all control paths"

// The only `ret` is inside a `while`, and the condition is false on entry here,
// so the loop body never runs and the function would fall off the end. A loop is
// not a guarantee: unless its condition is the literal `true`, the code after it
// is reachable and the function still needs a return there.
//
// This is the case that says the check may not ask whether the loop's *body*
// returns — only whether the loop can be left. 28_a_loop_followed_by_a_return.cpl
// is the accepted form, with a `ret` after the loop for the run that never enters
// it, and 29_while_true_returns_from_inside.cpl is the one loop that does count.

fn f n
    while n > 0
        ret 1

fn main
    out "{f(0)}"
